<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69580" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶμαι</span></b> , 
			Med.
		, 3sg.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					117
				</span></i>
			; 3pl.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euph.
					157
				</span></i>
			; imper. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶσο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					[288]
				</span></i>
			 (corr. Ahrens), prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; 3sg. opt. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῷτο</span> Diotog ap.<i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				3.1.100
			</span></i>; inf.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					771
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				406a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				7.219a
			</span></i>; part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μώμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					45
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				441
			</span></i> (both lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1136
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OC</u>
				836
			</span></i> (lyr.): aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμώσατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			:—<i>seek after, covet</i>, c. acc., <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
			</span></i> l.c., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀκριβές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diotog.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ λανθάνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.: c. inf. or abs., <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> ll.cc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>meditate</i> or <i>purpose</i>, c. acc., <i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i> ll.cc. (Non-thematic <i>mō</i>-, prob. cogn.
			with Lat. <i>mōs</i> 'will', 'caprice'; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαίομαι</span>.)</div>
